---
import DocPage from '../../components/DocPage.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
---
<DocPage eyebrow="GUIDE / VISUAL TESTING" title="Visual testing guide" lead="Gua.Testing.Visual compares screenshots from a running game with reviewed PNG baselines to detect overlap, clipping, layout shifts, wrong assets, themes, and other defects that can remain even when semantic controls exist and behave correctly. It provides engine-independent visual regression coverage for the rendering contract that semantic assertions cannot prove." description="Gua.Testing.Visual use cases, baseline workflow, comparison settings, artifacts, masks, variants, and CI." section="visual-testing">
  <Callout kind="tip" title="Game-engine independent"><p><code>Gua.Testing.Visual</code> consumes an <code>IGuaContext</code> and the PNG in Gua diagnostics, so the same API and baseline workflow applies to Godot, Unity, and custom adapters. Only screenshot capture and legitimate baseline variants differ by engine environment.</p></Callout>
  <h2>When it adds value</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Use visual comparison for</th><th>Prefer semantic assertions for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Clipping, overlap, and layout shifts</td><td>Control existence and visibility</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong textures, fonts, themes, or overlays</td><td>Expected text and values</td></tr><tr><td>Resolution-dependent layout breakage</td><td>State transitions after actions</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <Callout kind="tip" title="Use both"><p>Visual comparison complements semantic tests. Add it only to screens where appearance is part of the contract.</p></Callout>

  <figure class="doc-figure"><div class="flow"><span>Stable UI frame<small>optionally wait</small></span><b>→</b><span>Actual PNG<small>from diagnostics</small></span><b>→</b><span>Reviewed baseline<small>name + variant</small></span><b>→</b><span>Pixel comparison<small>threshold + masks</small></span><b>→</b><span>PASS / artifacts<small>review differences</small></span></div><figcaption>Figure 1: The baseline is selected by test name and variant; failures preserve all comparison evidence.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2>Install</h2><CodeBlock title="Add to a visual test project" lang="powershell" code={`dotnet add package Gua.Testing.Visual --version 0.14.0`} />

  <h2>Create a baseline deliberately</h2>
  <CodeBlock title="Allow a local baseline update" lang="powershell" code={`$env:GUA_UPDATE_BASELINES = "1"
dotnet test tests/Game.Visual.Tests/Game.Visual.Tests.csproj
Remove-Item Env:GUA_UPDATE_BASELINES`} />
  <p>Review the generated PNG and commit it only when it is correct. Never set this variable in an ordinary pull-request job.</p>

  <h2>Compare in normal test runs</h2>
  <CodeBlock title="Compare the title screen" lang="csharp" code={`using Gua.Testing.Visual;

var result = await GuaVisualAssertions.ExpectScreenshotAsync(
    host.Context, "title-screen", new ScreenshotOptions
    {
        BaselineDirectory = Path.Combine(TestContext.CurrentContext.TestDirectory, "baselines"),
        ArtifactDirectory = Path.Combine(TestContext.CurrentContext.WorkDirectory, "artifacts", "gua"),
        BaselineVariant = "windows-unity-mono-1920x1080",
        PixelThreshold = 0.02f,
        MaxDifferentPixelRatio = 0.001,
        WaitForStableSnapshot = true,
        StableFrames = 3,
    });`} />
  <p><code>PixelThreshold</code> tolerates small per-channel differences; <code>MaxDifferentPixelRatio</code> limits how many pixels may differ. Tune them only from known stable renderer noise.</p>

  <h2>Failure evidence</h2>
  <div class="artifact-row"><div><strong>expected.png</strong><small>reviewed baseline</small></div><div><strong>actual.png</strong><small>current capture</small></div><div><strong>diff.png</strong><small>visualized difference</small></div><div><strong>comparison.json</strong><small>policy, ratio, paths</small></div></div>
  <p>Set <code>FailureDirectory</code> to place visual artifacts beside ordinary Gua diagnostics. Dimension mismatches fail without implicit resizing.</p>

  <h2>Variants, masks, and stability</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Good use</th><th>Avoid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>BaselineVariant</code></td><td>Name legitimate OS, renderer, and resolution differences</td><td>Creating a variant for every failure</td></tr><tr><td><code>Masks</code></td><td>Exclude a clock or truly random avatar</td><td>Masking important UI</td></tr><tr><td><code>WaitForStableSnapshot</code></td><td>Capture after several stable frames</td><td>Baselining an arbitrary animation frame</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <CodeBlock title="Mask one nondeterministic region" lang="csharp" code={`Masks = new[]
{
    new GuaMaskRectangle(X: 1710, Y: 24, Width: 180, Height: 48), // clock only
};`} />

  <h2>CI policy</h2>
  <CodeBlock title="Upload failure artifacts" lang="yaml" code={`- name: Run visual tests
  shell: pwsh
  run: dotnet test tests/Game.Visual.Tests/Game.Visual.Tests.csproj --configuration Release

- name: Upload visual failures
  if: failure()
  uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
  with:
    name: gua-visual-failures
    path: artifacts/gua
    if-no-files-found: ignore`} />
  <p>Keep resolution, DPI, fonts, locale, theme, engine version, renderer, and GPU/driver policy deterministic. Separate baseline updates from ordinary CI and require review of the PNG diff.</p>
</DocPage>
